"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nThe body of a four-year-old girl is found, and her family along with a stranger become suspects.  \nEven though the child was murdered, they are more concerned with denying their own charges than grieving.  \n\nThe culprit changes every time the suspects are investigated.  \nAfter finishing this book, I felt like I had watched the show Crime Scene.  \n\nIt's a typical trick and culprit hunt, but the content is meticulous and has many elements of twists, so I enjoyed it.  \nIt's the kind of book that reads easily and quickly because you're curious about the whole story.  \nI felt once again that a character diagram is important for books like this."